> 
> The modest award is meant as a token acknowledgement more than anything
> else.  It's so if two players play a similar game, one with a conduct
> and another without, the conduct player will rank higher.  But players
> who are going for conducts are, in a way, beyond score.  Maybe what we
> need is an alternate vanity board, one that just lists ascensions,
> without score, and their conducts.

We have a token acknowledgement in the listing of "Voluntary Challenges" 
at the end of the game. A score bonus would have to be more than 
"modest" in order to have any effect, because no two games will be 
similar enough to be an "all things being equal" situation. As you also 
say in your original post, conducts are actually (usually) foolish 
playing styles used by experienced players to add to difficulty; it's 
the equivalent of "one hand tied behind my back." The score table 
shouldn't reward that; the bragging rights are already there for those 
who choose the conduct.
